# Keep the build context lean: deps are reinstalled, and the build output is
# regenerated inside the image. rootfs/ IS needed (it's COPYied in the runtime stage).
node_modules
dist
dist.zip
.git
.github
.env
*.log
.vite
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
villa-kiosk
MODEL_PIPELINE.md
CLAUDE.md
tests
# ⚠️ EXCEPT THE GATES `npm run build` ITSELF RUNS. `prebuild` runs the service
# worker's lifecycle oracle, because a throw from a vite plugin hook is
# swallowed by this bundler and the only place a non-zero exit is honoured is a
# script. Excluding all of tests/ therefore made `RUN npm run build` fail inside
# the image with the file simply absent — a gate added to protect the build,
# breaking it. They are tiny, they never reach the final image (only /app/dist
# is copied out of the build stage), and keeping them here means the image is
# built by the same command, with the same checks, that a developer runs.
!tests/oracles
!tests/consistency

# Model pipeline working files (source GLBs, SweetHome exports, Blender
# intermediates) — 1.6GB+ locally, gitignored, and never read by the
# Dockerfile. Without this, a local `docker build` sends the whole thing to
# the daemon AND copies it into the build stage via `COPY . .`, on every
# build. CI is unaffected (sources/ is untracked, so it's never checked out),
# but this matters for the "Local build fallback" path in README.md.
sources

# Python bytecode (supervisor-proxy.py) — rootfs/ IS copied into the image, so
# without this a stale local __pycache__/*.pyc would get baked in too.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# ⚠️ THE VILLA'S OWN VOCABULARY AND THE LOCAL TLS KEYS. .gitignore protects both
# and this file did not know about either. On the "Local build fallback" path
# above, `COPY . .` bakes .scratch/forbidden-tokens.txt — the villa's name,
# hostname and model filename, the exact strings tests/hard-rules.py exists to
# keep out of a public repo — and any mkcert private key into the build stage.
# They do not reach the final image (only /app/dist is copied out), but
# build.yaml exports every stage with `cache-to: type=gha,mode=max`, so those
# bytes would land in a shared build cache. CI is safe only by the accident
# that actions/checkout cannot produce an untracked file — which is the same
# accident that makes the token check SKIP there.
.scratch
certs
